    "retrospective_semester": 8,
    "citation": "IITK_Minor_Courses_Catalogue.md section 1 (DOAA / UG Manual guidelines)",
    "text": "A Minor consists of 3 to 4 courses worth 27 to 36 credits. Minor course credits are counted against the Open Elective requirements of the student's primary degree template. B.Tech, BS and Dual Degree (Category A) students may apply for a Minor in any department except their own. No global CPI floor is mandated by DOAA, but departmental selection committees frequently enforce CPI cutoffs and seat caps."
  },
